  message: "Withdrawn 2026-05-08 — original filing was based on hg-uat-v4.1.0 Round 08 §8.4's 'WI-vigih transitive walk observably vacuous' framing, which orchestrator source-read on 2026-05-08 established was a misreading of the linker's two-step design.\n\nThe corrected analysis (full detail in master-report.md §4 DQ-3 revised; summary here):\n\nview-template-linker-v1 has two distinct steps documented in its module docstring (view_template.py:4 'Rails controllers render view templates by convention'; function docstring view_template.py:185 'convention-based view templates'; transitive-walk comment view_template.py:195-198):\n\n- Step 1 (controller identification): transitive base-class walk via _transitive_bases.collect_transitive_base_names against _CONTROLLER_BASES = {ApplicationController, ActionController::Base, ActionController::API}. Gates which classes count as Rails controllers.\n- Step 4 (template resolution): file-system probe at app/views/<controller-path>/<action>.<ext>. Emits the renders edges.\n\nRound 08 §8.4's probe measured Step 4 only ('does the walk affect template resolution?' — answer: no, by design) and concluded the walk was 'vacuous'. That conclusion was wrong. The walk is observably load-bearing for Step 1: without it, all 12 of Round 06's ground-truthed transitive cases would fail at controller identification (their direct bases are project-internal intermediates not in _CONTROLLER_BASES — Api::V1::Accounts::BaseController, Public::BaseController, SuperAdmin::ApplicationController). Round 06's 'moved' verdict is fully dependent on the walk.\n\nThe SuperAdmin coverage that Round 08 cited as evidence of 'inheritance NO + view file YES → edge emitted' was actually 'inheritance YES via inheritance.py's short-name fallback + view file YES → edge emitted'. inheritance.py's qualified-name lookup at lines 175-194 falls back to short-form lookup when the qualified form is third-party; Administrate::ApplicationController gets resolved to chatwoot's own bare ApplicationController (a confidence=0.5 fallback edge per INV-zuhub), and the BFS reaches ActionController::Base in the chain. Step 1 succeeds. Round 08's 'inheritance NO' premise was incorrect.\n\nThere is no claim-vs-behavior reconciliation needed: the linker is correct as-shipped, the docstring is correct, and WI-vigih's transitive walk is observably load-bearing for Step 1. Architecturally, the convention-based Step 4 is the only mechanism that captures Rails' implicit-render semantics (other web frameworks dispatch on AST-visible explicit render() calls; Rails dispatches by filename at runtime regardless). Each web-framework's view-resolution linker should mirror its framework's actual runtime dispatch.\n\nOptional low-priority docstring polish (NOT being filed as a follow-up — orchestrator can decide later if the master report revision isn't enough): add an explicit 'Step 1 vs Step 4: two mechanisms for two questions' subheading to view_template.py's module docstring, plus a brief note that the BFS walk relies on inheritance.py's short-name fallback for chains passing through third-party gems (Administrate-shaped). Would prevent future readers from making the same misreading the master report's first draft did.\n\nReferences:\n- Master report §4 DQ-3 (revised): ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_artifacts/hg-uat-v4.1.0/lab-notebook/master-report.md\n- Source: packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/view_template.py:4, :185, :195-198, :199-209\n- Property tests pinning Step 1 transitive walk: packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_view_template_linker.py:511, :547\n- inheritance.py short-name fallback: packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/inheritance.py:175-194\n- Round 06 ground-truth narrative: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_artifacts/hg-uat-v4.1.0/lab-notebook/round-06-WI-vigih-view-template-transitive/report.md\n- Round 08 §8.4 probe (now superseded by source-read analysis): ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_artifacts/hg-uat-v4.1.0/lab-notebook/round-08-followup-discriminators/report.md"  # bbf5
